        "title": {
          "en": "The shopping list"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Amma wrote: bananas, apples, grapes and milk.\n\"The commas keep each item apart,\" she said."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "comma",
          "quotation marks",
          "paragraph"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A comma separates items in a list: I like mangoes, grapes and apples. No comma is needed before and.\nQuotation marks show the exact words someone says: Ravi said, \"I am hungry.\" The spoken words go inside the marks.\nA paragraph is a group of sentences about one idea. Start a new paragraph for a new idea."
        }
